####################################################################
# hierarchy.ttl — HAND-AUTHORED.  NOT GENERATED.
#
# Every curated "is a narrower case of" placement between vocabulary
# concepts, in one reviewable place. Created in the p99 curation round
# (2026-11-24); before that these edges were split over vocab_base.ttl (value
# states) and inference.ttl (ECG group types, CPAP).
#
# This file PLACES concepts; it does not define them. The concepts come from
# the annotated CSV, vocab_base.ttl or inference.ttl, as before. A concept
# named here and nowhere else gets a generated stub (and is listed in the
# build log, so a typo does not pass silently).
#
# build_framework.py merges this file into vocab_generated.ttl — consumers
# load that file and never this one, so no loader can forget it. Per edge it
# also writes skos:broader (replacing the default edge to the scheme's top
# concept), so SKOS tools that do not reason show the same tree.
#
# THREE SECTIONS, THREE CLAIM KINDS
#
#   A. Value refinements    mda:refinesConcept, within one scheme.
#      For concepts used as the VALUE of a property (states). Through the
#      property chains in ontology.ttl ("Concept refinement"), a node
#      bearing the narrower value is entailed to bear the broader one.
#
#   B. Kind subclassing     rdfs:subClassOf, within one scheme.
#      For concepts used as the TYPE of a node (sensor, signal, therapy).
#      OWL-RL inherits along it natively.
#
#   C. Cross-scheme links   skos:broadMatch.
#      A value in one scheme that falls under a value in ANOTHER scheme
#      (borne by a different property). Not entailed — for queries
#      ((skos:broader|skos:broadMatch)*) only.
#
# RULES FOR AN EDGE (apply before adding one)
#   - "Every X is always a Y." If that does not hold in every case, it is
#     not a refinement.
#   - Synonyms are MERGED in the annotation, never nested: nesting two names
#     for one state makes them look like two meanings.
#   - Annotators record the most specific value the label supports, never
#     the child and its parent together; the parent is entailed.
####################################################################

@prefix mda:              <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#> .
@prefix rdfs:             <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix opstate:          <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/operation-state/> .
@prefix qualitystate:     <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/quality-state/> .
@prefix metricValueState: <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric-value-state/> .
@prefix metricRhythm:     <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric-rhythm/> .
@prefix sensor:           <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/sensor/> .
@prefix signal:           <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/signal/> .
@prefix signalAnalysis:   <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/signal-analysis/> .
@prefix therapeuticModality: <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/therapeutic-modality/> .


####################################################################
# A. Value refinements (mda:refinesConcept)
####################################################################

# ── Quality state (signal; also therapy delivery) ────────────────────
# Impaired is the general "this signal cannot be relied on"; its
# refinements name the cause the alarm label gives. An alarm whose label
# gives no cause stays plain Impaired.
#
# OutOfRange ("buiten bereik": outside the device's measuring range) placed
# under Impaired (2026-11-25): a signal outside the range the device can
# measure cannot be relied on, so an alarm resting on it is suspect (CAT1a).
# Not placed yet, pending a decision: ScalingError ("wijzig schaal"), which
# concerns the display range rather than the signal itself.
qualitystate:OutOfRange    mda:refinesConcept  qualitystate:Impaired .
qualitystate:Pulseless     mda:refinesConcept  qualitystate:Impaired .
qualitystate:Weak          mda:refinesConcept  qualitystate:Impaired .
qualitystate:Interference  mda:refinesConcept  qualitystate:Impaired .
# Unanalyzable (2026-11-25, p99 "PHILIPSMONITOR - Niet te leren ECG"): the
# device states it cannot analyse the signal, without naming a cause and
# without naming which outputs of the analysis are lost. A narrower case of
# Impaired, so rules written against Impaired also cover it.
qualitystate:Unanalyzable  mda:refinesConcept  qualitystate:Impaired .

# ── Metric value state ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Moved from vocab_base.ttl. A severe deviation is a narrower case of the
# deviation in its direction: "the same direction and not more severe" is
# `?active skos:broader* ?incoming` (an active SeverelyDecreased covers an
# incoming Decreased, not the other way round; the two directions share no
# ancestor below ValueState). Now also ENTAILED: a SeverelyIncreased metric
# bears Increased, so axioms keyed on Increased (the circuit-leak therapy
# delivery axiom in inference.ttl) fire for the severe case too — before
# this they silently did not.
metricValueState:SeverelyDecreased  mda:refinesConcept  metricValueState:Decreased .
metricValueState:SeverelyIncreased  mda:refinesConcept  metricValueState:Increased .

# ── Metric rhythm ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Abnormal: a rhythm that is present but not normal. Scheme-neutral on
# purpose (the rhythm scheme serves respiration too), so not "Arrhythmia".
# Absent is NOT under it: an absent rhythm is the extreme low of the value
# (section C), not an abnormal pattern of a present one.
metricRhythm:Fibrillation  mda:refinesConcept  metricRhythm:Abnormal .
metricRhythm:Tachycardia   mda:refinesConcept  metricRhythm:Abnormal .
# Ventricular rhythms (2026-11-25, p99 ECG fix 3). VF and VT name where the
# fibrillation or tachycardia arises. VentricularFibrillationOrTachycardia is
# what "PHILIPSMONITOR - Ventrikel Fibr/Tachy" states: one of the two, not
# which. Deliberately not "VentricularArrhythmia", which would be wider than
# the label (it would also cover e.g. ventricular ectopy).
metricRhythm:VentricularFibrillationOrTachycardia  mda:refinesConcept  metricRhythm:Abnormal .
metricRhythm:VentricularFibrillation  mda:refinesConcept  metricRhythm:Fibrillation ,
                                                          metricRhythm:VentricularFibrillationOrTachycardia .
metricRhythm:VentricularTachycardia   mda:refinesConcept  metricRhythm:Tachycardia ,
                                                          metricRhythm:VentricularFibrillationOrTachycardia .

# ── Operation state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unavailable: temporarily not measuring, without being broken (warming
# up, purging, an interrupted measurement). Disabled (switched off by the
# user) is deliberately not placed here yet: that is a choice, not a
# transient condition.
#
# Synonyms merged in the annotation instead of nested (2026-11-24):
# Failure -> Malfunction, Unconnected -> Disconnected.
#
# Malfunction: the component is not working as it should, so what it
# produces cannot be used. Its refinements name the fault the alarm label
# gives (2026-11-25, decided with the CAT1a review: a sensor in any of
# these states is not acquiring its signal). Unrecognized is placed here
# too: whether the sensor is faulty or the wrong one, it is not delivering.
opstate:AdapterFault     mda:refinesConcept  opstate:Malfunction .
opstate:MCableFailure    mda:refinesConcept  opstate:Malfunction .
opstate:PositionalError  mda:refinesConcept  opstate:Malfunction .
opstate:Unrecognized     mda:refinesConcept  opstate:Malfunction .
opstate:Initializing  mda:refinesConcept  opstate:Unavailable .
opstate:Cleaning      mda:refinesConcept  opstate:Unavailable .
opstate:Interruption  mda:refinesConcept  opstate:Unavailable .


####################################################################
# B. Kind subclassing (rdfs:subClassOf)
####################################################################

# ── ECG group types ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Moved from inference.ttl (ECG section of the FunctionalUnit recipes,
# where the electrode/lead wiring they group still lives).
#
# The supertype every ECG electrode and every ECG signal shares. These are
# not new concepts: they are the two the researchers were already annotating
# with (sensor:ElectroCardioGraphy_sensor on "ECG afleidingen los" / "ECG
# alle leads los", signal:ECG_signal on "ECG artefact"), given a formal place
# rather than left denoting a whole with no relation to its parts.
# (2026-11-25: the artefact alarms now name signal:ECG_lead instead, see
# DATA/ANNOTATION/TODO_ecg_annotation_fixes.md, fix 1. ECG_signal stays as
# the umbrella kind over the raw signals and the leads, which reach it
# through ECG_raw_signal / ECG_lead below.)
#
# Their job is to keep a per-alarm node HONEST when the trace is not
# determined. Without them, an ECG heart-rate alarm asserted "hasSensor [ a
# mda:Sensor ]" — the ontology's top sensor class, which a pulse oximeter
# satisfies just as well as an electrode. build_framework.py's
# _shared_supertype() reads these edges (from this file) to say "some ECG
# electrode" instead: exactly what the alarm evidences and nothing more.
#
# Expressed as subtyping rather than as a SensorGroup entity with a part-of
# property: a group here is a KIND of sensor, not a thing that has members,
# so no new class or property is needed and existing queries over mda:Sensor
# keep working unchanged.
sensor:ECG_RA_sensor rdfs:subClassOf sensor:ElectroCardioGraphy_sensor .
sensor:ECG_LA_sensor rdfs:subClassOf sensor:ElectroCardioGraphy_sensor .
sensor:ECG_LL_sensor rdfs:subClassOf sensor:ElectroCardioGraphy_sensor .
sensor:ECG_RL_sensor rdfs:subClassOf sensor:ElectroCardioGraphy_sensor .
sensor:ECG_V1_sensor rdfs:subClassOf sensor:ElectroCardioGraphy_sensor .
sensor:ECG_V2_sensor rdfs:subClassOf sensor:ElectroCardioGraphy_sensor .
sensor:ECG_V3_sensor rdfs:subClassOf sensor:ElectroCardioGraphy_sensor .
sensor:ECG_V4_sensor rdfs:subClassOf sensor:ElectroCardioGraphy_sensor .
sensor:ECG_V5_sensor rdfs:subClassOf sensor:ElectroCardioGraphy_sensor .
sensor:ECG_V6_sensor rdfs:subClassOf sensor:ElectroCardioGraphy_sensor .
# The respiration electrode(s) of impedance pneumography (2026-11-25;
# inference.ttl, impedance section): physically ECG electrodes, so a state
# on the group covers them, but their own particular, so an alarm on them
# reaches only the impedance pathway. Their signal is deliberately NOT
# under ECG_raw_signal: it feeds no lead derivation, and the impedance
# signal it yields is not an ECG signal.
sensor:ECG_Resp_sensor rdfs:subClassOf sensor:ElectroCardioGraphy_sensor .

# The raw signals and leads used to be listed here as direct subclasses of
# ECG_signal too; removed 2026-11-25 as redundant with the kinds below. The
# thoracic impedance signal (formerly ECG_lead_Impedance, then a direct
# subclass of ECG_signal) is NOT an ECG signal: a separate measurement on
# the same electrodes. It has no kind here (inference.ttl, impedance
# pneumography).

# Kinds below ECG_signal (p99 curation round, 2026-11-24). signal:ECG_lead
# is what the heart-rate, arrhythmia and ST analyses take as input
# (inference.ttl): "an ECG lead", which lead being device configuration.
# (ECG_raw_signal was also the placeholder input of the thoracic impedance
# derivation until 2026-11-25; that input is now ECG_Resp_signal from
# sensor:ECG_Resp_sensor, below.) ECG_raw_signal and
# ECG_lead_derivation exist so that an alarm on such an analysis gets an
# honest node per layer of its chain ("some ECG raw signal", "some lead
# derivation") rather than the bare ontology class. The thoracic impedance
# signal and its derivation measure something else and stay outside the
# ECG_signal and ECG_lead_derivation kinds.
signal:ECG_raw_signal rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_signal .
signal:ECG_lead       rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_signal .
signal:ECG_RA_signal rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_raw_signal .
signal:ECG_LA_signal rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_raw_signal .
signal:ECG_LL_signal rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_raw_signal .
signal:ECG_V1_signal rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_raw_signal .
signal:ECG_V2_signal rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_raw_signal .
signal:ECG_V3_signal rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_raw_signal .
signal:ECG_V4_signal rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_raw_signal .
signal:ECG_V5_signal rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_raw_signal .
signal:ECG_V6_signal rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_raw_signal .
signal:ECG_lead_I   rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_lead .
signal:ECG_lead_II  rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_lead .
signal:ECG_lead_III rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_lead .
signal:ECG_lead_aVR rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_lead .
signal:ECG_lead_aVL rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_lead .
signal:ECG_lead_aVF rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_lead .
signal:ECG_lead_V1  rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_lead .
signal:ECG_lead_V2  rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_lead .
signal:ECG_lead_V3  rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_lead .
signal:ECG_lead_V4  rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_lead .
signal:ECG_lead_V5  rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_lead .
signal:ECG_lead_V6  rdfs:subClassOf signal:ECG_lead .

signalAnalysis:ECG_derivation_I   rdfs:subClassOf signalAnalysis:ECG_lead_derivation .
signalAnalysis:ECG_derivation_II  rdfs:subClassOf signalAnalysis:ECG_lead_derivation .
signalAnalysis:ECG_derivation_III rdfs:subClassOf signalAnalysis:ECG_lead_derivation .
signalAnalysis:ECG_derivation_aVR rdfs:subClassOf signalAnalysis:ECG_lead_derivation .
signalAnalysis:ECG_derivation_aVL rdfs:subClassOf signalAnalysis:ECG_lead_derivation .
signalAnalysis:ECG_derivation_aVF rdfs:subClassOf signalAnalysis:ECG_lead_derivation .
signalAnalysis:ECG_derivation_V1  rdfs:subClassOf signalAnalysis:ECG_lead_derivation .
signalAnalysis:ECG_derivation_V2  rdfs:subClassOf signalAnalysis:ECG_lead_derivation .
signalAnalysis:ECG_derivation_V3  rdfs:subClassOf signalAnalysis:ECG_lead_derivation .
signalAnalysis:ECG_derivation_V4  rdfs:subClassOf signalAnalysis:ECG_lead_derivation .
signalAnalysis:ECG_derivation_V5  rdfs:subClassOf signalAnalysis:ECG_lead_derivation .
signalAnalysis:ECG_derivation_V6  rdfs:subClassOf signalAnalysis:ECG_lead_derivation .

# Cardiac output by thermodilution (Swan-Ganz) is one method of computing
# cardiac output; the generic step stays the one an alarm uses when the
# method is unknown (inference.ttl, Swan-Ganz trace; p99 curation round).
signalAnalysis:ThermodilutionAnalysis rdfs:subClassOf signalAnalysis:CardiacOutputAnalysis .

# ── Therapeutic modality ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Moved from inference.ttl. CPAP is a mode of ventilation therapy (decision
# 38): as a subclass it inherits VentilationTherapy's targetsProcess and the
# therapy-delivery-quality axioms scoped to VentilationTherapy (leak,
# malfunction, disconnected circuit). Consumers that match rdf:type without
# reasoning (MDA-POC) must follow rdfs:subClassOf* to see it.
therapeuticModality:CPAP rdfs:subClassOf therapeuticModality:VentilationTherapy .


####################################################################
# C. Cross-scheme links (skos:broadMatch) — query-time only
####################################################################

# Moved from vocab_base.ttl. An absent rhythm (asystole, apnoea) is the
# extreme low of the metric's value: linked across schemes, so it sits below
# SeverelyDecreased in the value-state hierarchy without leaving the rhythm
# scheme. Not entailed: hasRhythm Absent does not become hasValueState
# SeverelyDecreased (that would change the property, not just the value).
metricRhythm:Absent  skos:broadMatch  metricValueState:SeverelyDecreased .
